From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:31:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 25/35] PROTOTYPE pvr: only 32-bit formats take the linear
 window-size rule

Local fix to 3b79e00da87 for amazon-suez, never to be sent. Linear R8
images sample wrong: Firefox uploads software-decoded video as three R8
planes, and with them linear the video showed at half size in the top-left
quadrant with the rest clamped (or garbled). Exempting 1-byte formats fixed
it, 2 of 2 runs each way. The window-sized buffers the rule is for are all
32-bit (RGBA8, D24S8/D32), so keep it to those; 8, 16, 64 and 128-bit
formats stay twiddled.

Generated-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit c171569ba236c20d4b6d803db45833174a35015d)
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c
index f7614994fb0..4870ff3d4c5 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c
@@ -62,6 +62,14 @@ static bool pvr_image_twiddle_padding_is_wasteful(const struct pvr_image *image)
        image->vk.array_layers > 1 || image->vk.samples > VK_SAMPLE_COUNT_1_BIT)
       return false;
 
+   /* Only 32-bit texels: the window-sized buffers this is for are RGBA8 and
+    * D24S8/D32. A linear R8 image samples wrong here (Firefox's software-
+    * decoded video planes came out at half size, the rest clamped), and the
+    * other sizes are untested.
+    */
+   if (vk_format_get_blocksize(image->vk.format) != 4)
+      return false;
+
    return util_next_power_of_two64(w) * util_next_power_of_two64(h) * 4 >
           w * h * 5;
 }
